  "question": {
    "text": "<p>A zener diode of power rating <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>1</mn><mo>.</mo><mn>6</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">W</mi></math>&nbsp;is to be used as voltage regulator. If the zener diode has a breakdown of <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>8</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">V</mi></math> and it has to regulate voltage fluctuating between <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>3</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">V</mi></math> and <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>10</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">V</mi></math> The value of resistance <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mi>R</mi><mi>s</mi></msub></math> for safe operation of diode will be</p><p><img src=\"assets\\qt0056_440fcd6d7d92.png\" style=\"width: 250px; height: 126px;\" /></p>"
  },
  "options": [
    {
